    "fullContent": "<p><strong>Meridian Remote Work &amp; Hybrid Work Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Company:</strong> Meridian<br /><strong>Policy Number:</strong> HR-017<br /><strong>Department:</strong> Human Resources<br /><strong>Version:</strong> 1.0<br /><strong>Status:</strong> Draft — For Review<br /><strong>Effective Date:</strong> To Be Confirmed<br /><strong>Policy Owner:</strong> To Be Confirmed</p><p><strong>1. Purpose</strong></p><p>This policy establishes guidelines for employees working remotely or following a hybrid work arrangement. It aims to support productivity, collaboration, information security, and work-life balance.</p><p><strong>2. Scope</strong></p><p>This policy applies to Meridian employees whose roles and approved work arrangements permit remote or hybrid work.</p><p><strong>3. Definitions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Remote Work:</strong> Performing assigned work from an approved location outside the company's usual workplace.</li><li><strong>Hybrid Work:</strong> Combining work from the office with work from an approved remote location.</li><li><strong>On-site Work:</strong> Performing assigned duties at the designated company workplace.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Eligibility and Approval</strong></p><p>Remote and hybrid work eligibility depends on job responsibilities, business requirements, team coordination, and management approval.</p><p>Employees must:</p><ul><li>Obtain approval through the applicable company process.</li><li>Follow their manager's instructions regarding work location.</li><li>Attend on-site meetings or activities when required by an approved work arrangement.</li><li>Follow any applicable attendance and work-from-home policy.</li></ul><p>Remote or hybrid work should not be assumed to be automatically available to every employee.</p><p><strong>5. Working Hours and Availability</strong></p><p>Employees must follow their assigned working hours and applicable attendance requirements.</p><p>During working hours, employees should:</p><ul><li>Remain reasonably available through approved communication channels.</li><li>Attend scheduled meetings.</li><li>Inform their manager about planned absences or significant availability issues.</li><li>Communicate delays that may affect assigned responsibilities.</li></ul><p>Any flexible working arrangements must follow the applicable approval process.</p><p><strong>6. Productivity and Performance</strong></p><p>Remote and hybrid employees are responsible for completing their assigned duties and meeting agreed objectives.</p><p>Managers should communicate expectations clearly and evaluate performance using relevant work outcomes, responsibilities, and established performance management procedures.</p><p>Employees should raise workload, access, or collaboration concerns promptly.</p><p><strong>7. Equipment and Workspace</strong></p><p>Employees must use authorized equipment and software for company work.</p><p>They should:</p><ul><li>Keep company equipment secure and in good working condition.</li><li>Maintain a workspace suitable for their assigned responsibilities.</li><li>Report lost, damaged, or malfunctioning company equipment through the designated process.</li><li>Follow applicable laptop, software installation, and IT support policies.</li></ul><p>Equipment eligibility, reimbursement, and return requirements are governed by the applicable company policies.</p><p><strong>8. Information Security and Privacy</strong></p><p>Remote employees must follow Meridian's information security and data protection requirements.</p><p>They should:</p><ul><li>Use approved systems and secure network connections.</li><li>Protect company devices from unauthorized access.</li><li>Avoid discussing confidential information where unauthorized individuals may overhear.</li><li>Lock devices when unattended.</li><li>Report suspected security incidents promptly.</li><li>Avoid storing company information on unauthorized personal devices or accounts.</li></ul><p><strong>9. Communication and Collaboration</strong></p><p>Remote and hybrid employees should maintain effective communication with colleagues and managers.</p><p>They are expected to:</p><ul><li>Participate in relevant team meetings.</li><li>Keep colleagues informed about important work progress.</li><li>Use approved company communication channels.</li><li>Document decisions and action items where necessary.</li><li>Respect colleagues' working hours and communication boundaries.</li></ul><p><strong>10. Health, Safety, and Well-being</strong></p><p>Employees should maintain a reasonably safe and suitable work environment.</p><p>They should report work-related safety concerns through the appropriate company channel and take reasonable breaks during the working day.</p><p><strong>11. Changes to Work Arrangements</strong></p><p>Changes to an approved remote or hybrid arrangement may require manager or HR approval.</p><p>Meridian may review arrangements based on business needs, role requirements, collaboration needs, or applicable company procedures.</p><p>Employees should not assume that an existing arrangement can be changed permanently without approval.</p><p><strong>12. Roles and Responsibilities</strong></p><p><strong>Employees</strong></p><ul><li>Follow approved work arrangements.</li><li>Meet work and communication expectations.</li><li>Protect company information and equipment.</li></ul><p><strong>Managers</strong></p><ul><li>Communicate responsibilities and availability expectations.</li><li>Review requests according to business needs.</li><li>Support team collaboration and performance.</li></ul><p><strong>Human Resources</strong></p><ul><li>Provide guidance on work arrangements.</li><li>Coordinate policy interpretation and review.</li></ul><p><strong>IT Team</strong></p><ul><li>Provide authorized tools and technical support.</li><li>Advise employees on secure remote access and equipment requirements.</li></ul><p><strong>13. Policy Violations</strong></p><p>Failure to follow this policy may be addressed under applicable company procedures, including attendance, conduct, performance, or information security policies.</p><p><strong>14. Frequently Asked Questions</strong></p><p><strong>Q1. Can every employee work remotely?</strong><br />No. Eligibility depends on role requirements, business needs, and approval.</p><p><strong>Q2. Can I change my remote working days?</strong><br />You should obtain approval according to the applicable company process.</p><p><strong>Q3. Do remote employees need to attend meetings?</strong><br />Yes, when the meetings are relevant to their responsibilities and attendance is required.</p><p><strong>Q4. What if my internet connection stops working?</strong><br />Inform your manager through an available communication channel and follow the applicable contingency process.</p><p><strong>Q5. Can I use my personal laptop for company work?</strong><br />Only if permitted by Meridian's IT and information security requirements.</p><p><strong>Q6. Who approves remote work?</strong><br />The designated manager or authorized approver under the company's official process.</p><p><strong>Q7. What if I need technical assistance while working remotely?</strong><br />Contact the designated IT support channel.</p><p><strong>Q8. Are remote employees exempt from attendance requirements?</strong><br />No. Applicable attendance and reporting requirements continue to apply.</p><p><strong>15. Review and Approval</strong></p><p>This is a draft policy template. Meridian must confirm eligibility criteria, approval authority, remote work schedules, equipment arrangements, and any location-specific requirements before publication.</p><p><strong>Approval Status:</strong> Pending Review<br /><strong>Approved By:</strong> To Be Confirmed<br /><strong>Effective Date:</strong> To Be Confirmed</p>"
