    "fullContent": "<p><strong>MERIDIAN</strong></p><p><strong>Software Installation and Approval Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Document ID:</strong> MER-IT-003<br /><strong>Version:</strong> 1.0 — Sample<br /><strong>Policy Owner:</strong> IT Operations and Information Security<br /><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 1 January 2026 (fictional)<br /><strong>Review Date:</strong> 1 January 2027 (fictional)<br /><strong>Classification:</strong> Internal Use Only<br /><strong>Approval Status:</strong> Draft — For Review</p><p><strong>1. Purpose</strong></p><p>This policy ensures that software used on Meridian devices is licensed, secure, compatible, and appropriate for business use.</p><p><strong>2. Scope</strong></p><p>This policy applies to employees, contractors, interns, administrators, and third parties who install or use software on Meridian-managed devices or access Meridian business data.</p><p><strong>3. Policy Statement</strong></p><ol><li>Only approved and appropriately licensed software may be installed on company-managed devices.</li><li>Employees must submit a software request through the IT service portal.</li><li>Business justification and manager approval are required for nonstandard software.</li><li>IT must review security, compatibility, licensing, privacy, and support requirements before approval.</li><li>Employees must not bypass administrative controls or use unauthorized installers.</li><li>Software must be obtained from approved vendors or trusted distribution channels.</li><li>Trial, freeware, open-source, and subscription-based products must still undergo the required review.</li><li>Unauthorized software may be removed when necessary to protect company systems.</li></ol><p><strong>4. Software Categories</strong></p><p><strong>Standard software:</strong> Preapproved applications available through the company software catalog.</p><p><strong>Business software:</strong> Applications requiring departmental justification and licensing review.</p><p><strong>Restricted software:</strong> Tools that create elevated security, privacy, compliance, or operational risks. These require specialist review and may be prohibited.</p><p><strong>Developer tools:</strong> Compilers, development environments, libraries, and related tools subject to approved engineering and security standards.</p><p><strong>5. Request Procedure</strong></p><ol><li>Open the Meridian IT service portal.</li><li>Select “Software Installation Request.”</li><li>Provide the software name, vendor, business purpose, required features, and device details.</li><li>Identify whether the software processes confidential, personal, or regulated information.</li><li>Obtain manager approval where required.</li><li>IT reviews licensing, security, privacy, compatibility, and support requirements.</li><li>The requester receives an approval, rejection, or request for additional information.</li><li>Authorized IT personnel install the software or provide access through the approved software catalog.</li><li>The requester confirms successful installation.</li></ol><p><strong>6. Roles and Responsibilities</strong></p><p><strong>Requester:</strong> Explain the business need and use the software only for authorized purposes.</p><p><strong>Manager:</strong> Validate business need and approve associated expenditure where applicable.</p><p><strong>IT Operations:</strong> Check compatibility, deploy software, and maintain supported versions.</p><p><strong>Information Security:</strong> Assess vulnerabilities, permissions, and data-handling risks.</p><p><strong>Procurement or Legal:</strong> Review licensing, contractual terms, and vendor conditions when necessary.</p><p><strong>7. Sample Service Targets</strong></p><ul><li>Standard catalog installation: Within two business days.</li><li>New software assessment: Within five business days after complete documentation is received.</li><li>High-risk or procurement-dependent requests: Timeline provided after specialist review.</li></ul><p>These are illustrative targets, not guaranteed turnaround times.</p><p><strong>8. Frequently Asked Questions</strong></p><p><strong>Q1. Can I install free software without approval?</strong><br />No. Free software may still present security, privacy, licensing, or compatibility risks. Use the approved catalog or submit a request.</p><p><strong>Q2. What if I need software urgently for a client meeting?</strong><br />Submit an urgent request with the deadline and business justification. IT will prioritize it where feasible, but security checks cannot be bypassed.</p><p><strong>Q3. Can I use a personal software license on a company laptop?</strong><br />Only if the license permits business use and Meridian approves the arrangement.</p><p><strong>Q4. What happens if unauthorized software is detected?</strong><br />IT may restrict or remove it, investigate the circumstances, and refer the matter to Information Security if necessary.</p><p><strong>Q5. Can I install browser extensions?</strong><br />Only extensions permitted under Meridian's browser and security standards may be used.</p><p><strong>9. Escalation Instructions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Level 1 — IT Helpdesk:</strong> Standard installation, catalog access, or installation errors.</li><li><strong>Level 2 — IT Application Support:</strong> Compatibility issues, licensing errors, or specialized application requirements.</li><li><strong>Level 3 — Information Security or Software Asset Management:</strong> Suspected malicious software, licensing violations, data-security concerns, or prohibited tools.</li></ul><p>Report suspected malware immediately. Disconnect from the network only when instructed by the incident-response team or the applicable emergency procedure.</p><p><strong>Sample contact:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:software.support@meridian.example\">software.support@meridian.example</a> | <a href=\"mailto:security@meridian.example\">security@meridian.example</a></p><p><strong>10. Exceptions</strong></p><p>Exceptions require a written justification, documented risk review, and approval from the IT Manager and Information Security where applicable. Approval may be time-limited and subject to additional controls.</p><p><strong>11. Compliance</strong></p><p>Unauthorized installation, license misuse, or circumvention of security controls may result in software removal, access restrictions, or further action under applicable company procedures.</p><p><strong>12. Revision History</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Version</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Date</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1.0</p></td><td><p>1 January 2026</p></td><td><p>Initial fictional sample draft</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"
